Here is a high-level software architecture comparison and technical blueprint for implementing the programmer in either **Web Audio API + WebAssembly (AudioWorklet)** or **JUCE (C++)**.

---

## 1. Stack Comparison & Recommendation

| Criteria | Web Stack (Web Audio + WebAssembly / C++) | Desktop Native (JUCE C++) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Target Deliverable** | Web app, browser-based generator, PWAs | VST3 / AU / AAX plugin, standalone app |
| **DAW Integration** | Limited (MIDI export, Web MIDI out, virtual cabling) | Native sample-accurate DAW clock/MIDI drag-and-drop |
| **Real-time Performance** | Excellent via `AudioWorkletNode` + Wasm | Industry standard, zero-garbage-collection C++ |
| **File I/O & Storage** | Web File System Access API, IndexedDB | Direct filesystem access, native sample playback |

* **Choose Web Audio API** if your primary goal is rapid distribution, zero-install accessibility, web-based MIDI export/generation, or cross-platform browser deployment.
* **Choose JUCE C++** if your primary goal is an in-DAW VST3/AU plugin with sample-accurate host synchronization, multi-out routing, and native CPU performance.

