## 4. JUCE C++ Architecture Spec

### Class Structure

```
MyPercussionEngine/
├── Source/
│   ├── PluginProcessor.h/cpp   <-- AudioProcessor (Host sync, MIDI out)
│   ├── PluginEditor.h/cpp      <-- AudioProcessorEditor (JUCE UI)
│   ├── Engine/
│   │   ├── SequencerEngine.h   <-- Pattern evaluation & tempo lock
│   │   ├── Humanizer.h         <-- Timing drift, jitter & velocity curves
│   │   └── StateMachine.h      <-- Hat openness (0.0 to 1.0) & choke groups
│   ├── Audio/
│   │   ├── SampleVoice.h       <-- Individual playback voice DSP
│   │   └── SamplerSound.h       <-- Multi-zone sample mapping (Tip/Shank)
│   └── Utils/
│       └── LockFreeQueue.h     <-- Producer/Consumer thread-safe buffers

```

### Key Technical Considerations

* **Sample-Accurate Host Sync:** Use `juce::AudioPlayHead` within `processBlock()` to query tempo, time signature, and transport position (`ppqPosition`).
* **Choke Group Implementation:** When a closed hi-hat event triggers, iterate active voices in the same choke group and execute a fast decay envelope ($2\text{--}5\text{ ms}$) to prevent audio pops while stopping the voice.
* **Lock-Free Messaging:** Use `juce::AbstractFifo` or `farbot::fifo` to pass parameter updates from the Editor thread to the Processor thread without lock contention.

