## 5. Hi-Hat State Engine Data Model

Below is a state tracking model applicable to both C++ and TypeScript:

```typescript
interface PercussionEvent {
  step: number;               // Step index (e.g., 0-15 for 16th notes)
  instrumentId: string;       // e.g., "hihat", "cabasa", "agogo"
  subdivision: number;        // 1 = normal, 2 = 32nd roll, 4 = 64th roll, etc.
  velocity: number;           // 0.0 - 1.0
  timingOffsetMs: number;     // Micro-timing offset (-20ms to +20ms)
  hatOpenness: number;        // 0.0 (Tight Closed) to 1.0 (Full Open)
  pitchShiftSemitones: number;// e.g., -12 to +12 for Trap rolls
  pan: number;                // -1.0 (Left) to +1.0 (Right)
}

```

